{
  "an4.192:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.192 ",
  "an4.192:0.2": "20. The Great Chapter ",
  "an4.192:0.3": "Facts ",
  "an4.192:1.1": "“Mendicants, these four things can be known in four situations. ",
  "an4.192:1.2": "What four? ",
  "an4.192:1.3": "You can get to know a person’s ethics by living with them. But only after a long time, not casually; only when attentive, not when inattentive; and only by the wise, not the witless. ",
  "an4.192:1.4": "You can get to know a person’s purity by dealing with them. … ",
  "an4.192:1.5": "You can get to know a person’s resilience in times of trouble. … ",
  "an4.192:1.6": "You can get to know a person’s wisdom by discussion. But only after a long time, not casually; only when attentive, not when inattentive; and only by the wise, not the witless. ",
  "an4.192:2.1": "‘You can get to know a person’s ethics by living with them. But only after a long time, not casually; only when attentive, not when inattentive; and only by the wise, not the witless.’ ",
  "an4.192:2.2": "That’s what I said, but why did I say it? ",
  "an4.192:2.3": "Take an individual who’s living with someone else. They come to know: ",
  "an4.192:2.4": "‘For a long time this venerable’s deeds have been broken, tainted, spotty, and marred. Their deeds and behavior are inconsistent. ",
  "an4.192:2.5": "This venerable is unethical, not ethical.’ ",
  "an4.192:3.1": "Take another individual who’s living with someone else. They come to know: ",
  "an4.192:3.2": "‘For a